    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors). The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is support.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature. When a create request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, an owner sharing an existing owner's last name + address is now allowed (instead of a 409), and all members of that household are stamped with the same stable `householdId`, which is returned on the owner.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it (MapStruct auto-maps it by name).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `household_id` column to the `owners` table in all four `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` files (hsqldb is the one the tests use).\n\n4. **`rest/function/owner/CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java`** \u2014 reworked the existing check. It now collects existing same-lastName/same-address owners:\n   - No match \u2192 proceed (lone owner).\n   - Match but `sharesHousehold` not true \u2192 409 `DuplicateHouseholdException` (unchanged behaviour).\n   - Match and `sharesHousehold` true \u2192 derive a **stable** household id (reuse one an existing member already carries, else deterministically `\"H-\" + SHA-256(lastNameKey + \"\\n\" + addressKey)`), stamp it on the new owner and on every existing member (saving those). Because it's derived from the normalized household key, independent joiners compute the identical value, so `SaveOwner`/`RespondWithOwnerCreated` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` return matching `householdId`s.\n\nThe derivation reuses the existing normalized comparison key (lower-cased, whitespace-collapsed) so the household id tracks the same owners the duplicate check already groups together.",
